<title>SINGAPORE: Silk Air to fly to 2nd Philippines city.</title>
<headline>Silk Air to fly to 2nd Philippines city.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Silk Air, the regional wing of Singapore Airlines Ltd, said on Friday it would operate a twice-weekly direct service to Davao City in the southern Mindanao region of the Philippines from March 1997.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement Davao City would be its second destination in the Philippines, after Cebu.</p>
<p>The flights would depart Singapore every Wednesday and Sunday, it said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
